# ── LLM Provider ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THIS FILE IS THE DEVELOPER FALLBACK, NOT THE NORMAL WAY TO CONFIGURE A KEY.
# The normal route is the app's Settings screen, which saves to
# .curator-config.json (permissions 0600). A key saved there ALWAYS out-ranks
# the same provider's variable here.
#
# Two consequences worth knowing before you rely on a key in this file:
#   • Saving a key in Settings also makes that provider the ACTIVE one
#     (last-saved-wins), and the active provider is what runs ingest, Wiki
#     Health and Compile.
#   • A key that lives ONLY here does not appear in the chat model picker.
#     That is deliberate: a provider you Disconnected in Settings must not stay
#     usable in chat.
#
# Set at least one key below. If several are present and nothing has been chosen
# in Settings, the first one in this order wins: Gemini, Anthropic, OpenRouter.
#
# Option A: Google Gemini  (recommended — very low cost)
#   Get key: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_key_here
#
# Option B: Anthropic Claude
#   Get key: https://console.anthropic.com
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_key_here
#
# Option C: OpenRouter  (one key onto many vendors; cheapest route to building
#           a wiki, and one of its offered models is free)
#   Get key: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your_openrouter_key_here

# ── Model override (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Affects the ACTIVE provider only — a provider that is not active ignores it.
# It is an unrestricted developer escape hatch and is NOT checked against the
# active provider's own catalogue, so an id belonging to a different provider
# gets paired with the active one and fails at the API. Use an id from the
# active provider's list. Current defaults:
#   Gemini:     gemini-2.5-flash-lite
#   Anthropic:  claude-haiku-4-5
#   OpenRouter: upstage/solar-pro4
# LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite

# ── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=3333

# ── Knowledge Base Location (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────
# By default, The Curator looks for a "domains" folder inside the app directory.
# Set DOMAINS_PATH to an absolute path if your wiki lives somewhere else —
# for example a dedicated folder that has its own private GitHub sync repo.
#
# Examples:
#   DOMAINS_PATH=/Users/yourname/Documents/my-brain
#   DOMAINS_PATH=/Users/yourname/Dropbox/curator-wiki
#
# Leave commented out to use the default ./domains folder.
# DOMAINS_PATH=

# ── Sync (set automatically by the Sync tab — do not edit manually) ───────────
# These are written by the app when you configure sync via the UI.
# GITHUB_SYNC_REPO and token are stored in .sync-config.json (gitignored).
